# CHG-2028 (approved): the source is held to a monthly budget (AWS Budgets, alerting its paging channel) and the target
# was set up without one, which the planner blocks on: hold the target to its own, 25000 USD a month, alerting its
# paging action group at 80% and 100% spent and 100% forecast. Once its quota limits were fetched (CHG-2026), the target's
# region grants 50 vCPUs where its environments need 96: the operator takes the planner's fix with its approve option
# (fix quota:prod:vcpus: request what the environments need), so the increase is requested at 96. Azure has no
# Terraform resource for it: the target's root names the request, and the planner asks for the quotas to be fetched
# again once Microsoft grants it.
dn: cn=monthly-spend,ou=bindings,env=prod,cloud=target,ou=environments,dc=ciam-ops
changetype: add
objectClass: top
objectClass: ciamBudget
cn: monthly-spend
ciamBindingRole: budget
ciamBudgetAmount: 25000
ciamCurrency: USD
ciamBudgetPeriod: monthly
ciamActualThreshold: 80
ciamActualThreshold: 100
ciamForecastThreshold: 100
ciamAlertRole: alerts-page
ciamOwner: cn=ciam-platform,ou=owners,dc=ciam-ops
ciamChangeRef: cn=CHG-2028,ou=changes,dc=ciam-ops

dn: cn=quota-vcpus,ou=bindings,env=prod,cloud=target,ou=environments,dc=ciam-ops
changetype: modify
replace: ciamQuotaDecision
ciamQuotaDecision: request
-
replace: ciamQuotaRequested
ciamQuotaRequested: 96
-
replace: ciamChangeRef
ciamChangeRef: cn=CHG-2028,ou=changes,dc=ciam-ops
